  "text": "Orikalka - Basic Guide\n\n​\nGeneral Information\n⬥ Orikalka has 190,000 LP, across a single fight phase\n⬥ Orikalka primarily attacks with Melee , with some Magic  attacks\n​\nOther guides: #rex-matriarchs #unknown-channel\n​\nGear, Relics and Familiars\nExample Preset  \n​\n\nFight Mechanics\n⬥ Stay aware of nearby Matriarchs when moving, as only 3/4 Matriarchs share the main arena\n⬥ You should attack with Magic \n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Fire spells  give a +27% hit chance boost\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Any other style will only deal insignificant damage\n​\nAttack Rotation\n3x  → Frost Storm →  →  → Pyroclastic Shock →\n3x  → Pyroclastic Shock →  → 2x  → Pyroclastic Shock →\n2x  →  → Pyroclastic Shock → 3x  → Pyroclastic Shock →  →\nRepeat\n​\nAuto Attacks (Melee example / Magic example)\nMechanic: Orikalka uses Melee  and Magic  auto attacks.\n​\nSolution:\n⬥ If lower Defence  pray against Melee  / \n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Pray  once you are comfortable surviving the mechanics\n​\nFrost Storm / Frostbite (Example)\nMechanic: Orikalka spins in place, dealing up to 4500 Magic  damage and applying Frostbite.\nWhile Frostbite is active, your global cooldown is doubled for 30 seconds. This makes your abilities feel much slower and lowers your damage.\n​\nSolution:\n⬥ If Frost Storm deals too much damage, use  /  or \n⬥ If you get Frostbite, either:\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Keep fighting with abilities which don't care about the global cooldown (e.g., channels  /  or damage-over-time abilities )\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Clear it using the fissures from Pyroclastic Shock (see below)\n​\nPyroclastic Shock / Fissures (Example)\nMechanic: Orikalka slams its tail, creating 3 fissures on the ground. Standing on a fissure deals rapid Melee  damage, with the final hit dealing up to 6000 damage.\n​\nSolution:\n⬥ Avoid the fissures unless you are attempting to clear Frostbite (see above solution under Frost Storm)\n​\nHelpful videos\n⬥ Example kills with Revo++\n​\n\n      \n    ",
  "normalizedText": "Orikalka - Basic Guide ​ General Information ⬥ Orikalka has 190,000 LP, across a single fight phase ⬥ Orikalka primarily attacks with Melee , with some Magic attacks ​ Other guides: #rex-matriarchs #unknown-channel ​ Gear, Relics and Familiars Example Preset ​ Fight Mechanics ⬥ Stay aware of nearby Matriarchs when moving, as only 3/4 Matriarchs share the main arena ⬥ You should attack with Magic ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Fire spells give a +27% hit chance boost ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Any other style will only deal insignificant damage ​ Attack Rotation 3x → Frost Storm → → → Pyroclastic Shock → 3x → Pyroclastic Shock → → 2x → Pyroclastic Shock → 2x → → Pyroclastic Shock → 3x → Pyroclastic Shock → → Repeat ​ Auto Attacks (Melee example / Magic example) Mechanic: Orikalka uses Melee and Magic auto attacks. ​ Solution: ⬥ If lower Defence pray against Melee / ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Pray once you are comfortable surviving the mechanics ​ Frost Storm / Frostbite (Example) Mechanic: Orikalka spins in place, dealing up to 4500 Magic damage and applying Frostbite. While Frostbite is active, your global cooldown is doubled for 30 seconds. This makes your abilities feel much slower and lowers your damage. ​ Solution: ⬥ If Frost Storm deals too much damage, use / or ⬥ If you get Frostbite, either: ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Keep fighting with abilities which don't care about the global cooldown (e.g., channels / or damage-over-time abilities ) ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Clear it using the fissures from Pyroclastic Shock (see below) ​ Pyroclastic Shock / Fissures (Example) Mechanic: Orikalka slams its tail, creating 3 fissures on the ground. Standing on a fissure deals rapid Melee damage, with the final hit dealing up to 6000 damage. ​ Solution: ⬥ Avoid the fissures unless you are attempting to clear Frostbite (see above solution under Frost Storm) ​ Helpful videos ⬥ Example kills with Revo++ ​",
